om snapshot` cites `test_replay_from_snapshot_plus_tail_reconstructs_state` at `recovery_tests.rs:21`. |\n55\t\n56\t### Documentation coverage\n57\t\n58\tAll eleven items from spec §Documentation Requirements map to a delivered file with the required headings:\n59\t\n60\t1. Successor architecture overview — `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-successor-architecture-overview.md` (`## Overview` present)\n61\t2. MCP contract reference — `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-mcp-tool-reference.md` (T61)\n62\t3. Memory model reference — `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-memory-model-reference.md`\n63\t4. Event log design — `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-event-log-design.md`\n64\t5. Consolidation design — `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-consolidation-design.md`\n65\t6. Retrieval/ranking design — `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-retrieval-ranking-design.md`\n66\t7. Verification/freshness design — `docs/architecture/2026-05-16-verification-freshness-design.md`\n67\t8. Operator guide — `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-operator-guide.md`\n68\t9. Migration guide from Lattice — `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-migration-from-lattice.md` (`## Migration steps` present)\n69\t10. Benchmark/evaluation guide — `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-benchmark-evaluation-guide.md`\n70\t11. Extension review UI guide — `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-extension-review-ui-guide.md`\n71\t\n72\tPlus R87-required:\n73\t- Runbook — `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-runbook.md` (`## Daily operations` present, deploy sequence matches CLAUDE.md verbatim)\n74\t- Recovery playbook — `docs/operator-guide/2026-05-16-recovery-playbook.md` (`## Recovery procedures` + `## Replay from snapshot` present, T82 cross-link present)\n75\t\n76\t### `baselines/large_repo_results.json` audit\n77\t\n78\t- 6 fixtures (`event-log-compaction`, `extra-large`, `large-polyglot`, `medium-typescript`, `payload-spillover`, `small-rust`) with up to 10 tools per fixture and 1000 samples per tool.\n79\t- **Zero P99 budget breaches** across the matrix. Tightest absolute margin: `payload-spillover:before` 6565 µs vs 10 ms budget (34% headroom). All `identity_resolution` paths ≤ 130 µs P99 against a 2 ms budget.\n80\t\n81\t## Issues encountered\n82\t\n83\t### F1 (in-scope, fixed) — flaky log capture in `corruption_tests`\n84\t\n85\t`test_truncated_event_log_file_reports_recovery_or_sqlite_error_without_panic` failed intermittently (~30–50% under parallel test execution; 0% with `--test-threads=1`) because `tracing`'s per-callsite Interest cache is keyed against the global subscriber, but `capture_logs` was installing a thread-local subscriber via `set_default`. Once another test's `tracing_subscriber::fmt::try_init()` installed a global default, the `info!` callsites in `EventStore::open` cached `Interest::Never` for the thread-local capture path. Rewrote `capture_logs` to use a process-wide global subscriber (installed once via `OnceLock`) that routes through a `ThreadLocalWriter`, restoring deterministic capture. 10/10 verification passes after fix; full hardening suite 43/43 pass.\n86\t\n87\t### F2 (out of R87 scope) — pre-existing unrelated failures in other phases\n88\t\n89\tThe broader `cargo test -p lattice-core --lib` run surfaced four failures unrelated to Phase 11:\n90\t\n91\t- `consolidation::deterministic_tests::duplicate_detector_emits_supersession_proposal` — passes in isolation; suggests Phase 6 test-ordering interference.\n92\t- `consolidation::deterministic_tests::scanners_route_through_runtime_without_direct_writes`\n93\t- `consolidation::session_tests::session_consolidation_hot_path_stays_under_five_milliseconds_p99`\n94\t- `events::tests::every_payload_serializes_deterministically` — payload fixture missing `post_apply_state_hash` field that was added to `MemoryConsolidated` payload.\n95\t\n96\tThese belong to R18 (events) / R47 (consolidation) and are flagged in the R87 review's Findings (F2) for R88 (definition-of-done) to track. They are not Phase 11 hardening regressions and do not block R87.\n97\t\n